1
00:00:11,080 --> 00:00:13,331
Do you think...

2
00:00:13,332 --> 00:00:18,629
Carabaos have dreams when they sleep?

3
00:00:20,381 --> 00:00:21,883
Of course.

4
00:00:22,633 --> 00:00:25,720
What do you think they dream of?

5
00:00:27,889 --> 00:00:31,476
The sweetest grass they can eat.

6
00:00:32,393 --> 00:00:34,687
Why do you ask?

7
00:00:36,439 --> 00:00:39,400
It looks like he's sleeping soundly.

8
00:00:42,862 --> 00:00:44,697
Bong.

9
00:00:45,865 --> 00:00:47,658
I have a question.

10
00:00:49,869 --> 00:00:51,870
What is it?

11
00:00:51,871 --> 00:00:53,914
But...

12
00:00:53,915 --> 00:00:56,876
Promise me you won't laugh.

13
00:00:59,796 --> 00:01:03,674
Now that you say it,
of course I am gonna laugh.

14
00:01:05,426 --> 00:01:08,387
I was just wondering.

15
00:01:11,724 --> 00:01:15,560
Gone is the day before
you can finish the question.

16
00:01:15,561 --> 00:01:17,271
Wait.

17
00:01:18,731 --> 00:01:21,109
I just want to know...

18
00:01:23,069 --> 00:01:25,780
if one of us...

19
00:01:27,198 --> 00:01:30,075
leaves the world first.

20
00:01:30,076 --> 00:01:32,536
What if I die?

21
00:01:32,537 --> 00:01:39,544
- Will you look for me?
- Yes.

22
00:01:52,557 --> 00:01:55,767
Our families expect us

23
00:01:55,768 --> 00:02:02,191
to marry someone
and raise a family.

24
00:02:04,652 --> 00:02:07,529
But first...

25
00:02:07,530 --> 00:02:13,451
our families expect us

26
00:02:13,452 --> 00:02:17,915
to make money.

27
00:02:19,500 --> 00:02:22,086
That is true.

28
00:02:23,796 --> 00:02:26,549
They expect a lot.

29
00:02:27,758 --> 00:02:32,179
Sometimes, I wish...

30
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:35,099
I wish it could always be like this.

31
00:02:38,519 --> 00:02:42,064
Like what?

32
00:02:44,734 --> 00:02:48,279
You and me, together.

33
00:02:54,535 --> 00:02:59,624
I think the carabao is getting jealous.

34
00:02:59,700 --> 00:03:05,500
"All the Things I Leave You"
(Episode 4)

35
00:03:42,124 --> 00:03:44,167
If he's the one to make my heart weak...

36
00:03:44,168 --> 00:03:46,629
Oh, I’d love it.

37
00:03:47,755 --> 00:03:50,465
And you have the guts to say.

38
00:03:50,466 --> 00:03:53,468
"The first one to fall, loses."

39
00:03:53,469 --> 00:03:54,469
Whatever.

40
00:03:54,470 --> 00:03:55,720
Look, Jorge.

41
00:03:55,721 --> 00:03:56,805
Handsome. Check.

42
00:03:56,806 --> 00:03:58,932
Smells good. Check.

43
00:03:58,933 --> 00:04:01,184
Knows how to dress. Check.

44
00:04:01,185 --> 00:04:03,645
Has a big...

45
00:04:03,646 --> 00:04:04,272
Ruth.

46
00:04:04,273 --> 00:04:05,897
- What?
- Stop it.

47
00:04:05,898 --> 00:04:08,650
I meant wallet.

48
00:04:08,651 --> 00:04:10,653
He has a big wallet.

49
00:04:12,488 --> 00:04:15,282
I said, he has a big wallet.

50
00:04:15,283 --> 00:04:19,078
You're thinking of something else.

51
00:04:20,955 --> 00:04:24,292
Oh, here's the other one.

52
00:04:32,425 --> 00:04:34,676
I brought something to cook.

53
00:04:34,677 --> 00:04:38,388
Isn't miki Grandpa Tino's favorite?

54
00:04:38,389 --> 00:04:39,764
How sweet.

55
00:04:39,765 --> 00:04:42,434
I wish he wasn't a cheater.

56
00:04:42,435 --> 00:04:43,768
- Ruth.
- Huh?

57
00:04:43,769 --> 00:04:44,894
Nothing!

58
00:04:44,895 --> 00:04:47,731
I said, sweet.

59
00:04:47,732 --> 00:04:50,610
I wish it was sweeter.

60
00:05:00,911 --> 00:05:01,787
Yeah.

61
00:05:01,787 --> 00:05:02,787
Wait.

62
00:05:04,957 --> 00:05:06,375
Miss me?

63
00:05:11,130 --> 00:05:13,340
Stupid.

64
00:05:13,341 --> 00:05:15,425
You disappeared.

65
00:05:15,426 --> 00:05:17,970
You disappeared too.

66
00:05:18,971 --> 00:05:20,722
I'm sorry.

67
00:05:20,723 --> 00:05:24,643
I had to do something.

68
00:05:25,770 --> 00:05:28,189
Is it Agnes?

69
00:05:29,690 --> 00:05:32,068
We're not together.

70
00:05:34,362 --> 00:05:38,074
Why are you lying about it?

71
00:05:38,908 --> 00:05:40,826
It's so obvious.

72
00:05:42,286 --> 00:05:44,079
We used to date.

73
00:05:44,080 --> 00:05:45,872
But...

74
00:05:45,873 --> 00:05:48,041
We're over now.

75
00:05:48,042 --> 00:05:50,419
Why don't you believe me?

76
00:05:51,087 --> 00:05:52,420
Why?

77
00:05:52,421 --> 00:05:54,173
You jealous?

78
00:05:55,675 --> 00:05:58,302
Why would I be jealous?

79
00:05:59,470 --> 00:06:01,596
You're clearly jealous.

80
00:06:01,597 --> 00:06:02,848
I’m not.

81
00:06:03,057 --> 00:06:04,600
Jorge?

82
00:06:05,434 --> 00:06:09,938
Your Grandpa Tino has a box
of jewelry in his room.

83
00:06:09,939 --> 00:06:11,899
Can you look for it?

84
00:06:12,108 --> 00:06:13,650
Now, Auntie?

85
00:06:13,651 --> 00:06:14,776
Yes, please.

86
00:06:14,777 --> 00:06:18,030
But don't tell Lilia, okay?

87
00:06:26,205 --> 00:06:27,956
I'll just look for it.

88
00:06:27,957 --> 00:06:31,418
Do you want to come
to the room with me?

89
00:06:31,419 --> 00:06:32,836
Hey!

90
00:06:32,837 --> 00:06:35,797
What will you do in the room again?

91
00:06:35,798 --> 00:06:38,216
Ruth, we'll look for...

92
00:06:38,217 --> 00:06:39,801
Kiko, come with me.

93
00:06:39,802 --> 00:06:40,803
Come on.

94
00:06:41,303 --> 00:06:42,345
To where?

95
00:06:42,346 --> 00:06:43,555
The kitchen.

96
00:06:43,556 --> 00:06:44,597
I have something to ask.

97
00:06:44,598 --> 00:06:47,725
What kind of miki do you want to cook?

98
00:06:47,726 --> 00:06:48,561
I’ll come too.

99
00:06:48,562 --> 00:06:52,481
No, you make coffee and serve them.

100
00:06:53,899 --> 00:06:57,193
What other kind of miki is there?

101
00:06:57,194 --> 00:06:58,821
Just follow me.

102
00:07:02,324 --> 00:07:03,117
What is it, Ruth?

103
00:07:03,118 --> 00:07:05,160
I have something to ask.

104
00:07:05,161 --> 00:07:06,286
Any kind works.

105
00:07:06,287 --> 00:07:07,662
It's not that.

106
00:07:07,663 --> 00:07:09,539
Do you like my cousin?

107
00:07:09,540 --> 00:07:10,540
Huh?

108
00:07:11,083 --> 00:07:13,669
I don't like liars.

109
00:07:15,963 --> 00:07:17,464
If I said yes,

110
00:07:17,465 --> 00:07:18,965
what will you do?

111
00:07:18,966 --> 00:07:20,216
Ha!

112
00:07:20,217 --> 00:07:22,261
For real?

113
00:07:24,722 --> 00:07:27,140
Wow, lobster.

114
00:07:27,141 --> 00:07:32,188
Oh, yeah. Someone wanted miki with lobster.

115
00:07:33,147 --> 00:07:37,151
The mayor’s son brought it... Nathan.

116
00:07:38,402 --> 00:07:39,361
For real?

117
00:07:39,362 --> 00:07:41,030
He's rich.

118
00:07:48,787 --> 00:07:50,538
Don't worry.

119
00:07:50,539 --> 00:07:53,166
Let's make your miki more delicious.

120
00:07:53,167 --> 00:07:55,835
Does it mean...

121
00:07:55,836 --> 00:07:57,755
You like me more?

122
00:07:58,923 --> 00:08:01,425
We'll see.

123
00:08:01,884 --> 00:08:03,719
Okay, let’s see.

124
00:08:04,053 --> 00:08:05,638
Insiong.

125
00:08:07,348 --> 00:08:08,307
Lilia.

126
00:08:08,308 --> 00:08:09,766
Look at your son.

127
00:08:09,767 --> 00:08:12,895
He and Kiko might be doing something.

128
00:08:13,729 --> 00:08:18,359
It might also be a reason why
he doesn't want to study in Manila.

129
00:08:19,360 --> 00:08:20,903
You may be wrong.

130
00:08:21,987 --> 00:08:27,742
Jorge probably believes

131
00:08:27,743 --> 00:08:31,497
that he will manage the restaurant.

132
00:08:35,084 --> 00:08:36,960
You're drunk, Insiong.

133
00:08:36,961 --> 00:08:39,004
Stop it.

134
00:08:40,339 --> 00:08:44,510
Keep in mind, Dad isn't here
anymore to solve your problems.

135
00:08:45,594 --> 00:08:47,845
And my god, this Jorge.

136
00:08:47,846 --> 00:08:51,308
I hope he makes the
right choice for his future.

137
00:08:53,060 --> 00:08:54,228
Lilia.

138
00:08:55,896 --> 00:08:57,773
What more do you want?

139
00:08:59,692 --> 00:09:00,859
Insiong.

140
00:09:03,279 --> 00:09:05,739
Hello, Mayor!

141
00:09:17,751 --> 00:09:21,630
- Having a good drink, are we?
- Good evening, Mayor.

142
00:09:22,881 --> 00:09:26,384
Thank you for visiting us.

143
00:09:26,385 --> 00:09:29,847
It's forbidden to say thanks at a wake.

144
00:09:30,723 --> 00:09:34,517
Oh no, the elders have so many beliefs

145
00:09:34,518 --> 00:09:41,275
that I don't even remember
it's bad to say thanks at a wake.

146
00:09:42,610 --> 00:09:47,322
It would be wrong not to visit
on the last night of the wake.

147
00:09:47,323 --> 00:09:51,826
We all know how much the migrant
farmers have helped our town.

148
00:09:51,827 --> 00:09:54,662
Yes, mayor. Thank you.

149
00:09:54,663 --> 00:09:55,956
Auntie.

150
00:09:58,500 --> 00:10:02,712
Is this really Nathan?
You look so handsome.

151
00:10:02,713 --> 00:10:06,549
I should've been the one to welcome you.

152
00:10:06,550 --> 00:10:09,802
You look so much like your father.

153
00:10:09,803 --> 00:10:11,095
Mayor, wait for a bit.

154
00:10:11,096 --> 00:10:13,557
Jorge!

155
00:10:14,183 --> 00:10:15,308
Jorge!

156
00:10:15,309 --> 00:10:16,476
This is urgent!

157
00:10:16,477 --> 00:10:18,728
Nathan's here!

158
00:10:18,729 --> 00:10:20,271
Oh, Nathan. This is Jorge.

159
00:10:20,272 --> 00:10:23,441
Jorge, this is Nathan.

160
00:10:23,442 --> 00:10:25,485
- Oh yeah, Auntie.
- Remember?

161
00:10:25,486 --> 00:10:28,780
We met back at the gate earlier.
He was waving at me.

162
00:10:28,781 --> 00:10:31,492
But I think he forgot who I am.

163
00:10:32,845 --> 00:10:34,179
How can I forget you?

164
00:10:34,203 --> 00:10:36,329
Yeah, I waved at you
because you were waving at me.

165
00:10:36,330 --> 00:10:37,455
Right?

166
00:10:37,456 --> 00:10:37,956
See?

167
00:10:37,957 --> 00:10:39,707
You already forgot.

168
00:10:39,708 --> 00:10:41,042
Don't you remember?

169
00:10:41,043 --> 00:10:43,295
When we were in kindergarten?

170
00:10:48,550 --> 00:10:50,802
Nat-Nat the Fat?

171
00:10:50,803 --> 00:10:53,638
See? Even up to now, you're still a bully.

172
00:10:53,639 --> 00:10:55,640
So it’s you.

173
00:10:55,641 --> 00:10:56,641
I didn't mean it.

174
00:10:56,642 --> 00:10:58,601
I just remembered.

175
00:10:58,602 --> 00:11:00,478
I remember only.

176
00:11:00,479 --> 00:11:02,730
Do I still deserve to be called that?

177
00:11:02,731 --> 00:11:04,274
Nat-Nat the Fat?

178
00:11:07,820 --> 00:11:08,779
Okay.

179
00:11:08,780 --> 00:11:10,071
I'll let you talk here.

180
00:11:10,095 --> 00:11:13,598
I'll leave you and I'm
going to help in there, okay?

181
00:11:16,245 --> 00:11:17,496
Kiko!

182
00:11:18,372 --> 00:11:19,915
Come help me here.

183
00:11:27,840 --> 00:11:32,260
Your bodyguards are intense.
Watching your every move.

184
00:11:32,261 --> 00:11:33,053
Of course.

185
00:11:33,054 --> 00:11:36,014
So if you bully me...
You already know.

186
00:11:39,685 --> 00:11:42,646
That was a long time ago.

187
00:11:43,856 --> 00:11:46,400
I'm only kidding, you know.

188
00:11:47,693 --> 00:11:49,360
You're not fat anymore.

189
00:11:49,361 --> 00:11:51,696
I mean, you're not fat.

190
00:11:51,697 --> 00:11:52,406
You're...

191
00:11:52,406 --> 00:11:52,906
Uh...

192
00:11:52,907 --> 00:11:55,909
You’re... What do you call it?

193
00:11:56,452 --> 00:11:58,996
What, handsome?

194
00:12:01,832 --> 00:12:03,083
A little bit.

195
00:12:03,542 --> 00:12:04,792
Wow!

196
00:12:04,793 --> 00:12:07,545
Your standards are so high.

197
00:12:07,546 --> 00:12:11,382
Maybe you're like that
with the people you like.

198
00:12:11,383 --> 00:12:12,383
No.

199
00:12:14,511 --> 00:12:16,387
So...

200
00:12:16,388 --> 00:12:19,433
Are you single?

201
00:12:22,728 --> 00:12:24,605
We should hang out sometime.

202
00:12:27,232 --> 00:12:30,944
Like play basketball or something, silly.

203
00:12:34,531 --> 00:12:36,700
Do you still know how to speak Ilocano?

204
00:12:37,576 --> 00:12:39,285
A little bit.

205
00:12:39,286 --> 00:12:40,287
No?

206
00:12:42,289 --> 00:12:44,465
Not anymore? Just...

207
00:12:45,375 --> 00:12:46,709
Even a little?

208
00:12:46,710 --> 00:12:48,212
A little.

209
00:12:57,638 --> 00:12:59,096
It's mine now.

210
00:12:59,097 --> 00:13:00,808
This one's expensive.

211
00:13:01,225 --> 00:13:02,391
- Do you like it?
- Expensive?

212
00:13:02,392 --> 00:13:03,935
- Yeah.
- C'mon.

213
00:13:03,936 --> 00:13:05,019
Do you want to try it?

214
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,562
Is it mine now?

215
00:13:06,563 --> 00:13:07,980
Yeah, you want to try?

216
00:13:07,981 --> 00:13:09,899
Of course, no problem.

217
00:13:09,900 --> 00:13:11,109
Okay.

218
00:13:15,864 --> 00:13:19,742
Wow, that looks nice on you.

219
00:13:19,743 --> 00:13:20,743
Nice?

220
00:13:20,744 --> 00:13:24,748
Yeah, this looks kinda nice on you.

221
00:13:25,332 --> 00:13:29,378
You can't even wear a jacket
in the Philippines but I like it.

222
00:13:33,215 --> 00:13:35,925
I hope you like...

223
00:13:35,926 --> 00:13:37,844
crumbs.

224
00:13:37,845 --> 00:13:41,139
Uh, I guess.

225
00:13:41,890 --> 00:13:43,975
Nathan, this is Kiko.

226
00:13:43,976 --> 00:13:45,477
Kiko, this is Nathan.

227
00:13:47,187 --> 00:13:50,356
He's my childhood friend and...

228
00:13:50,357 --> 00:13:51,400
We are...

229
00:13:52,401 --> 00:13:54,402
Why am I talking to you in English?

230
00:13:54,403 --> 00:13:58,281
Didn't Auntie give you something to do?

231
00:13:58,282 --> 00:14:00,032
Well?

232
00:14:00,033 --> 00:14:02,202
- Oh, right.
- You're just gonna stand there?

233
00:14:04,454 --> 00:14:08,500
I'll give this to you first and give this
back when you come back to the Philippines.

234
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,753
Yeah, yeah.
It's okay.

235
00:14:12,296 --> 00:14:13,671
Do you want some?

236
00:14:13,672 --> 00:14:15,841
I think this is mine.
I don't know.

237
00:14:16,216 --> 00:14:17,925
I'll just get you a new one.

238
00:14:17,926 --> 00:14:19,553
Okay.

239
00:14:46,830 --> 00:14:50,000
Who's jealous now?

240
00:14:51,501 --> 00:14:53,127
Me?

241
00:14:53,128 --> 00:14:54,838
Jealous?

242
00:14:56,506 --> 00:15:00,260
I know how kids from political clans act.

243
00:15:01,553 --> 00:15:05,473
They think they’re descended from gods.

244
00:15:05,474 --> 00:15:06,766
Hey.

245
00:15:06,767 --> 00:15:09,061
Nathan's a good guy.

246
00:15:15,943 --> 00:15:17,443
Hey!

247
00:15:17,444 --> 00:15:20,071
Be careful with those.

248
00:15:20,072 --> 00:15:22,782
Do you want Grandpa to haunt you?

249
00:15:22,783 --> 00:15:24,826
My bad.

250
00:15:42,094 --> 00:15:44,972
Grandpa Tino kept this all this time.

251
00:15:46,056 --> 00:15:49,350
When I made this for Grandpa Tino...

252
00:15:49,351 --> 00:15:52,645
It was the day he told me

253
00:15:52,646 --> 00:15:57,275
I'll manage the restaurant someday.

254
00:16:00,404 --> 00:16:02,072
Can I see?

255
00:16:04,241 --> 00:16:05,951
Look at me.

256
00:16:10,580 --> 00:16:13,041
Oh, it's Auntie.

257
00:16:15,043 --> 00:16:16,585
Jorge.

258
00:16:16,586 --> 00:16:18,671
If you think about it,

259
00:16:18,672 --> 00:16:22,801
your grandpa and grandma are together now.

260
00:16:23,468 --> 00:16:27,222
Maybe they're going on dates in heaven.

261
00:16:33,562 --> 00:16:35,813
Is it true...

262
00:16:35,814 --> 00:16:43,814
that the heart remembers even
when someone’s long gone?

263
00:16:45,699 --> 00:16:47,325
I don't know.

264
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:56,375
Jorge!

265
00:16:58,128 --> 00:17:01,757
This is what your aunt is looking for.

266
00:17:08,388 --> 00:17:10,390
Isn't it this one?

267
00:17:11,141 --> 00:17:12,600
Jorge!

268
00:17:12,601 --> 00:17:14,393
Come quick, your dad!

269
00:17:14,394 --> 00:17:15,854
Jorge!

270
00:17:21,735 --> 00:17:23,987
For my father!

271
00:17:26,114 --> 00:17:29,534
Good evening.

272
00:17:30,994 --> 00:17:33,454
Friends.

273
00:17:33,455 --> 00:17:37,209
And family.

274
00:17:38,627 --> 00:17:40,796
Tonight...

275
00:17:44,549 --> 00:17:45,716
Tonight,

276
00:17:45,717 --> 00:17:48,344
- We will get to know...
- Insiong!

277
00:17:48,345 --> 00:17:49,888
Stop it.

278
00:17:51,098 --> 00:17:53,308
Aren’t you ashamed?

279
00:17:54,184 --> 00:17:57,812
- Tonight, we will know...
- Insiong!

280
00:17:57,813 --> 00:17:59,522
How good...

281
00:17:59,523 --> 00:18:01,315
We will know how good my father was.

282
00:18:01,316 --> 00:18:04,778
Aren't you ashamed of what you're doing?

283
00:18:06,405 --> 00:18:07,656
Anyway.

284
00:18:13,912 --> 00:18:16,748
Stop for now.

285
00:18:18,083 --> 00:18:21,293
I will tell you...

286
00:18:21,294 --> 00:18:23,629
my side of the story.

287
00:18:23,630 --> 00:18:25,632
You know...

288
00:18:30,303 --> 00:18:33,472
My father

289
00:18:33,473 --> 00:18:36,184
loved me so much.

290
00:18:41,189 --> 00:18:43,400
Just like how

291
00:18:45,610 --> 00:18:47,946
he loved you all.

292
00:18:48,989 --> 00:18:51,116
Even Jorge.

293
00:18:53,410 --> 00:18:55,745
He loved Jorge

294
00:18:56,872 --> 00:18:59,373
far more than he loved me.

295
00:18:59,374 --> 00:19:01,710
But you know, Jorge...

296
00:19:03,378 --> 00:19:06,463
Your grandpa hated...

297
00:19:06,464 --> 00:19:08,967
your mom.

298
00:19:10,051 --> 00:19:12,053
Isn't he...

299
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:15,681
Because he thought,

300
00:19:15,682 --> 00:19:17,516
your mom was a whore.

301
00:19:17,517 --> 00:19:19,060
Dad.

302
00:19:25,066 --> 00:19:26,610
Father,

303
00:19:28,320 --> 00:19:31,239
did you even love me?

304
00:19:37,454 --> 00:19:40,790
You didn't even trust me.

305
00:19:44,085 --> 00:19:45,085
You know...

306
00:19:45,086 --> 00:19:46,545
Kiko, I can take care of this.

307
00:19:46,546 --> 00:19:47,713
- Insiong!
- Because...

308
00:19:47,714 --> 00:19:51,176
Insiong, stop that.
Aren't you ashamed?

309
00:19:52,260 --> 00:19:56,263
- Insiong, stop it!
- Because he thought so highly of himself!

310
00:19:56,264 --> 00:19:59,683
Stop it, Insiong.
Have some shame. Sit down.

311
00:19:59,684 --> 00:20:00,936
Dad.

312
00:20:05,148 --> 00:20:06,441
What?

313
00:20:06,983 --> 00:20:08,734
What, Jorge?

314
00:20:08,735 --> 00:20:11,238
Is that who you look up to?

315
00:20:14,824 --> 00:20:17,827
That's who you want to be like?

316
00:20:19,621 --> 00:20:21,331
Him!

317
00:20:22,457 --> 00:20:24,458
Insiong!

318
00:20:24,459 --> 00:20:26,043
Insiong, stop it.

319
00:20:26,044 --> 00:20:27,753
- Stop it, Insiong!
- Don’t touch me!

320
00:20:27,754 --> 00:20:29,381
Insiong, stop it.

321
00:20:33,635 --> 00:20:35,135
Let's go inside.

322
00:20:35,136 --> 00:20:36,429
Let's go.

323
00:20:45,605 --> 00:20:46,939
No!

324
00:20:46,940 --> 00:20:48,400
Insiong.

325
00:20:49,818 --> 00:20:53,488
- Stop it.
- A lot of people are watching.

326
00:20:54,698 --> 00:20:57,659
Insiong.
Come on.

327
00:21:00,829 --> 00:21:03,330
Stop it.

328
00:21:03,331 --> 00:21:04,666
Stop it.

329
00:21:12,590 --> 00:21:14,175
Ouchie!

330
00:21:14,926 --> 00:21:16,886
You're so dramatic.

331
00:21:17,345 --> 00:21:18,722
It hurts.

332
00:21:23,059 --> 00:21:24,894
Kiko.

333
00:21:26,187 --> 00:21:27,938
I just wondered.

334
00:21:27,939 --> 00:21:31,109
When you suggested that I study again...

335
00:21:36,323 --> 00:21:38,116
I thought of

336
00:21:39,492 --> 00:21:43,204
wanting to be a doctor.

337
00:21:45,332 --> 00:21:49,209
Your patient would suffer, doc.

338
00:21:49,210 --> 00:21:51,754
Your hands are too heavy.

339
00:21:51,755 --> 00:21:54,007
It's why I didn't push through.

340
00:21:56,176 --> 00:21:57,761
Jorge.

341
00:21:58,428 --> 00:22:00,347
The other day,

342
00:22:00,972 --> 00:22:06,561
I had the chance to
think about what you said.

343
00:22:08,188 --> 00:22:11,274
About the scholarship.

344
00:22:12,067 --> 00:22:13,777
What about it?

345
00:22:14,527 --> 00:22:15,778
I applied...

346
00:22:15,779 --> 00:22:16,780
Kiko!

347
00:22:17,739 --> 00:22:23,036
I'm sorry about what Insiong did.

348
00:22:24,204 --> 00:22:26,247
Yes, Auntie.
It's okay.

349
00:22:27,290 --> 00:22:30,085
Have you seen a jewelry box?

350
00:22:32,462 --> 00:22:36,256
If you see one, don't tell
your Auntie Camilla, okay?

351
00:22:36,257 --> 00:22:38,634
Just me.

352
00:22:38,635 --> 00:22:40,010
Jorge?

353
00:22:40,011 --> 00:22:42,347
Have you seen...

354
00:22:46,434 --> 00:22:49,478
I'm so concerned about Kiko.

355
00:22:49,479 --> 00:22:51,980
Are you okay now, Kiko?

356
00:22:51,981 --> 00:22:53,857
Yes, Auntie.
I'm okay.

357
00:22:53,858 --> 00:22:57,569
My god, Lilia.
I'm so worried for Kiko.

358
00:22:57,570 --> 00:22:59,780
It's why I'm here too.

359
00:22:59,781 --> 00:23:01,323
Poor kid.

360
00:23:01,324 --> 00:23:03,201
But he's okay now.

361
00:23:10,375 --> 00:23:13,336
Such a nice boy.

362
00:23:18,591 --> 00:23:23,053
It looks like they're competing
to be your favorite aunt.

363
00:23:23,054 --> 00:23:24,972
They smiled at me.

364
00:23:24,973 --> 00:23:26,598
Maybe...

365
00:23:26,599 --> 00:23:29,144
They’ll accept me now.

366
00:23:37,944 --> 00:23:41,739
This is what they were looking for.

367
00:23:48,788 --> 00:23:50,289
But...

368
00:23:50,290 --> 00:23:52,417
What's this one?

369
00:23:56,087 --> 00:23:58,465
Letters?

370
00:24:06,598 --> 00:24:08,683
Do you know him?

371
00:24:09,559 --> 00:24:11,143
No.

372
00:24:11,144 --> 00:24:15,565
But he looks familiar to me.

373
00:24:18,526 --> 00:24:21,738
You look like him.
No doubt about it.

374
00:24:44,177 --> 00:24:46,845
What's inside that box?

375
00:24:46,846 --> 00:24:48,514
Nothing, Auntie.

376
00:24:48,515 --> 00:24:50,057
Just pictures.

377
00:24:50,058 --> 00:24:52,018
Can I see?

378
00:24:53,811 --> 00:24:58,274
Who's Primitivo Pascual?

379
00:24:59,359 --> 00:25:00,567
Camilla!

380
00:25:00,568 --> 00:25:03,070
Yes, coming!

381
00:25:03,071 --> 00:25:06,615
Jorge, don’t forget the jewelry box.

382
00:25:06,616 --> 00:25:08,076
Yes, Auntie.

383
00:25:15,041 --> 00:25:17,626
Kiko.

384
00:25:17,627 --> 00:25:21,421
We can't read these here.

385
00:25:21,422 --> 00:25:23,758
Hide them for now?

386
00:25:26,553 --> 00:25:28,304
Let's meet tomorrow.

387
00:25:32,934 --> 00:25:35,144
Arrange them.

388
00:25:37,355 --> 00:25:39,648
You look like him.

389
00:25:39,649 --> 00:25:41,317
Let me see.

390
00:25:45,154 --> 00:25:47,949
You really look like him.

391
00:25:51,744 --> 00:25:53,663
Jorge.

392
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:02,422
My grandpa's name is Bong.

393
00:26:10,555 --> 00:26:13,390
“My world,”

394
00:26:13,391 --> 00:26:14,392
“Bong.”
